<title>UK: Shell London office sold to become flats.</title>
<headline>Shell London office sold to become flats.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>British property company Frogmore Estates, in partnership with builder Fairview New Homes Plc, said on Wednesday it had bought a 445,000 square feet central London office building from Shell Overseas Holdings Ltd, a unit of Royal Dutch/Shell, for conversion into flats.</p>
<p>The two firms, through their development company Riverside Developments (South Bank) Ltd, intend to create 382 residential flats in the block, known as the Shell Downstream Building, near London's Waterloo Station.</p>
<p>In a statement they said planning permission had been granted and Galliard Homes would be responsible for design and marketing of the apartments.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
